{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 37, :comments ["And it says <b>et your silver, etc.</b> Here it explains what is the נֶשֶׁךְ (bite/usury) and the תַּרְבִּית (excess/increase) that darken one's light. <b>Your silver (כַּסְפְּךָ)</b> — these are the things that a person craves (כּוֹסֵף) in this world for illusory things; <b>you shall not give him with neshech</b> — for when a person fulfills his bestial soul's desire and intoxicates his spirit through his cravings, he is bitten (נָשׁוּךְ) by this, and the venom of sin is cast into him. And it says <b>and with tarbit you shall not give your food</b> — meaning, even your food (אָכְלְךָ), which is something you were permitted to eat, you shall not increase (תַּרְבֶּה) in it, for when a person follows his throat and tilts the boundary of desire within it toward excesses, thereby he darkens the light of the soul, for when this rises, that falls: when felt desire increases, spiritual desire diminishes. And this is the verse's meaning (Proverbs 13:25): ״צַדִּיק אוֹכֵל לְשׂוֹבַע נַפְשׁוֹ״ — to the satiety of his soul, not for the pleasure of physical sensation. And its saying <b>I am YHWH</b>, etc., means: even though I say to you that I took you out of the land of Egypt to give you the land of Canaan — it is not to eat of its goodness and to be sated from its fruit that is the ultimate purpose, but rather לִהְיוֹת לָכֶם לֵאלֹהִים (to be a Elohim to you) — that is the essence of the land. And they said, of blessed memory, in Torat Kohanim, and this is their language: everyone who dwells in the land of Israel accepts upon himself the yoke of the kingdom of Heaven."], :book :leviticus, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 25, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T20:01:30.455827402Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}